  "symbol": "MSDL",
  "summary": "Morgan Stanley Direct Lending Fund is a business development company. It is a Private Debt fund. The fund specializes in senior secured term loans, first lien senior secureds (including unitranche loans), floating rate loans and second-lien senior secured term loans. The fund specializes in mezzanine debt, joint venture, unsecured debt, equity investments, leveraged buyouts, acquisitions, debt refinancings, recapitalizations and other opportunistic asset purchases. The fund chiefly invests in riskier bonds, issued by middle-market companies or by private equity firms looking to finance their acquisitions. The fund seeks to invest in software, IT services, insurance services, commercial services & supplies, health care providers & services, diversified consumer services, professional services, real estate management & development, automobile components and financial services. The fund seeks to invest in the United States. The fund seeks to invest in companies with EBITDA between $15 million and $200 million.",
